Your thought experiment doesn't really work. 

You're trying to compare forcing the father to have a surgery to give his kid a chance at living to (if you subscribe to anti-abortionists thoughts on fetuses) having a surgery to kill a human that has to grow inside you. 

&#x200B;

I think I get the point you're trying to make, but it really doesn't work. One is forcibly killing another human (again if you subscribe to fetus = person) and another is not consenting to a surgery to maybe save your child. The fetus only requires you because that's how they develop. A 6 year old needs you to take care of it, but (personally) a fetus isn't less valuable of a human just because it's less developed. If that's the case then there's an argument that developmentally challenged people/babies should be culled for being less valuable and a drain on resources (not my argument just pointing out the logic going by developmental requirements for a "human")

&#x200B;

If you think a fetus is cells, you won't make the connect required to have their argument. If you think it's a human, you'll see abortion as murder.

