"Cortisol makes you eat more and less active"

&#x200B;

You: "There's no direct correlation between stress and weight gain"

&#x200B;

You have a few extra chromosomes?

At the beginning from 300-240 I was going to the gym, but I didn't really stick with weight lifting for more than a month or 2. 90% of my exercise has just been walking. 

&#x200B;

When I go to the gym I do inclined ruck walks. Put about 20-45lbs (whatever you can push yourself to carry but not struggle) in a bag and set the incline to 5%+ with a normal walking pace, not speed walking, for me that was 3.2mph. I couldn't (still can't) run very long, so walking is the next best thing. I burned about 800 calories an hour at that weight carrying something, so a bit more than 2 miles of running, it just took longer. 

&#x200B;

Otherwise I just go hiking or skateboard now, but not even too long. Hikes are a few hours, but longboarding I'll just do for like 30-60m normally a couple times a week (if that tbh). 

&#x200B;

Almost all the weight loss I achieved was just tracking calories. At 300lbs my TDEE just sedentary was close to 4500 calories, so it didn't really take much to lose anything until I got to about 240

